      "id": 1,
      "text": "Milford, the town that includes Colliersville, was formed from Unadilla in 1796 as Suffrage before adopting its current name in 1800.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milford%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Susquehanna River winds south through Milford’s eastern side, gathering water from Cherry Valley Creek along the way.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milford%2C_New_York",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Milford sits northeast of Oneonta, placing it in the heart of Otsego County’s rolling hills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milford%2C_New_York",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The village of Milford lies within the town, while Milford Center, Portlandville, and Red Ridge Hill are nearby hamlets along NY‑28.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milford%2C_New_York",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "NY‑28 runs through Milford, intersecting NY‑7 in the town’s southern part, a historic crossroads for early settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milford%2C_New_York",
